WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.970 align:start position:0% line:0%
Today, we are testing
ourselves in the wind tunnel.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.273 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
- Let's hit it.
- ( fans whirring )

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.975 line:0%
Gav:<i> Well, that doesn't
 mess around!</i>

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:11.878
Dan:<i> That's a full 45
 right there.</i>

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.212 align:start size:69% position:31%
Why don't we start
testing some elements?

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:14.614
( wind blowing,
spraying )

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.882
Gav:<i> ( laughing )
 Look at that liquid!</i>

00:00:16.882 --> 00:00:17.917
<i> I brought my own balloon.</i>

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.018 align:start position:0%
It's a condom.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.719 align:start size:41% position:59%
( screaming )

00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:22.755
Gav:<i> That is the stupidest thing
 I've ever recorded</i>

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.392 align:start position:0%
in slow motion
in my life.

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.631 align:start position:0% line:0%
Well, that was a
beastly wind tunnel.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.800 align:start size:66% position:34% line:0%
It really was.
It was what? 80 miles
an hour?

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.535 align:start position:0% line:0%
Yeah. The shots of you
in the water,

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.169
especially 'cause we
backlit the water.

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:38.471
It just looked really cool.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.706
Like, it was fascinating
to see how the air

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:42.842
was moving around you,
but it also just looked wicked.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.444
It was like commercial grade
footage.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:46.279
You look like
a certain singer

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-<i> from a 90's music video.</i> 
-<i> ( Dan laughs )</i>

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:49.582
<i> ( R&amp;B music plays )</i>

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:52.118
Gav:<i> Oh, that's magic.</i>

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.253
<i> ♪ Yeah, yeah ♪</i>

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:59.325
I also think that you
condom sailing

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:02.929
on a skateboard might be
the most bizarre thing
we've ever shot.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:06.332
You know, that will be
one of the most fun things
I've done this year

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.966
- for sure.
- ( laughs )

00:01:07.966 --> 00:01:09.702 align:start position:0% line:0%
Something about your
flat hair,

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:13.673 align:start position:0% line:0%
with your smug face,
with that flapping
in the wind.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:15.708
<i> Goodness, gracious me.</i>

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:16.709 align:start size:56% position:44%
I didn't expect it
to work

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:17.710 align:start size:56% position:44%
and then it worked

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.711 align:start size:59% position:41%
and I was so happy.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.013 align:start size:59% position:41%
It was so much fun.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.513 align:start position:0%
Well, we thought it'd
be a good idea

00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:23.216 align:start position:0%
to learn a little bit
about the facility

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.750 align:start position:0%
so we talked to a bloke
who works there called Kevin.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.985 align:start size:66% position:34%
Let's kick it to Kev.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.121 align:start size:72% position:28% line:0%
- Dan:<i> Kevin.</i> 
-<i> Hi, Dan.</i>

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.724 line:0%
Hey, so you're one of the
aerodynamicists at Mira, right?
Have I got that right?

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.259 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- That's right.
- Yeah. That's a cool
  job title.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.460 align:start position:0%
Damn good occupation.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.661 align:start size:53% position:47%
So what does that
actually mean?

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:36.863 align:start size:63% position:38%
Like what do you do?

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:59% position:41%
So, one of the jobs
I have here

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:42.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
is to essentially characterize
how vehicles behave

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.702 align:start size:59% position:41%
from an aerodynamic
point of view

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:46.672 align:start size:72% position:28%
in terms of drag, lift,
front lift, rear lift.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:49.708 align:start position:0%
So what are some of
the fastest speeds of wind
you've seen in this tunnel?

00:01:49.708 --> 00:01:52.878 align:start size:81% position:19%
Um, so we can-- we usually
operate up to about
80 miles an hour.

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:55.014 align:start position:0%
And that's like equivalent
to like a hurricane or
something?

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.449 align:start size:78% position:22%
- Uh, um--
- Light hurricane?

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.151 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Yeah, a light hurricane.
- A light hurricane?

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
- A breezy hurricane.
- They can go quite strong.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.956 align:start size:59% position:41%
So, how do you feel
about the fact that

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:06.492 align:start size:75% position:25%
you're an aerodynamicist
with a PhD,

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.193 align:start size:56% position:44%
and does very
scientific things,

00:02:08.193 --> 00:02:10.296
and we come along,
whip out a condom,

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.131
<i> and fly along the floor
 with a skateboard.</i>

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.467 align:start position:0%
You have this huge
scientific facility,

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.935 align:start position:0%
you know, do you mind?
Is that--

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.104 align:start size:75% position:25%
Well, from an engineer's
point of view,

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.638 align:start size:63% position:38%
I kind of have to be
very professional

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:21.740 size:81% position:59%
about everything and that
basically makes my day job

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.209 align:start size:53% position:47%
a little bit dry,

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.879 align:start size:84% position:16%
so to have something
interesting happen for once

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.447 align:start size:63% position:38%
makes for quite
a nice change, so...

00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:30.783 align:start position:0%
And I bet in the-- what?
70, 60 year history
of this place...

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.351
Kevin:<i> Yup.</i>

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:33.719
Gav:<i> ...It probably not had been
 done before that.</i>

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:34.921 align:start size:69% position:31%
You may have very well
set a record there.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.522
Yes.

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start position:0%
It's quite an honor
that you lasted in it,
to be honest.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.425
That is great.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.093
Thanks very much, Kevin,
for letting us mess around
in here.

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:42.461 align:start size:81% position:19%
- No, thank you.
- It's a real honor.

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:44.797
Thanks a lot.
That was really so much fun.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.466 align:start size:88% position:13%
- That was a lot of fun.
- Glad you had fun.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:48.768 align:start position:0%
All right, back to you,
Gav and Dan.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.235 align:start position:0%
Oh, thanks, us.

00:02:50.235 --> 00:02:51.737 align:start position:0%
It's amazing how many
of the things we filmed

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.639
is so heavily influenced
by aerodynamics.

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.241
It's not just things
we film though,

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.309
I remember I used to ride
my bike to school,

00:02:57.309 --> 00:02:58.644
one day it was really windy

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.012
I was, like,
ten minutes late for school,

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:01.481
so as I walked into
the class,

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.182
and the teacher was like,
why are you late?

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:04.617
and I was like,
"It was windy."

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.486
And she just goes,
"Get out."

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.120
And the class just
laughed at me.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.223
Did you get laughed at
a lot as a kid?

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.558
Let's-- ( stammers )
Let's leave that, all right?

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:13.926 align:start size:69% position:31%
To find out more about
aerodynamics,

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:15.862 align:start size:56% position:44%
and why I was late
for school,

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:18.163 align:start size:78% position:22%
we've brought on someone
who is clearly never late
for school,

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:20.199 align:start size:75% position:25%
Lisa, who's an aerospace
engineer.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.601
- Thanks for coming.
- Thank for having me.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.269 align:start position:0%
Hello. Were you ever
late to school?

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.937 line:0%
- Oh, no, definitely not.
- Gav: Definitely not.

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:27.373 align:start position:0% line:0%
I'd love to get
your opinion on some
of the aerodynamics

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.241 align:start position:0%
of Dan and I,
so why don't we go over
to the screen...

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:30.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Sounds good.
- ...and have a little look.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Okay, first clip.
- The idea behind that was,

00:03:33.712 --> 00:03:34.947
it was that I was trying
to sit down fully,

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.582
<i> 90 degrees with my legs,</i>

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:38.551 align:start position:0%
but I couldn't do it
unless I had that little
bit extra

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.019 align:start position:0%
where I put my hands out
to help me...

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.220 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Makes sense.
- To get a bit more...

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.655
Yeah, just a little bit
more track.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.657 align:start size:91% position:9%
It was amazing the difference
that this made.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:47.260 align:start position:0%
- Mm-hmm.
- Gav: Over here what I'm doing
  is I was holding 

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.761
<i> my lab coat out,
 and I was trying to make</i>

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:50.929
<i> forward progress
 and the more I had it open</i>

00:03:50.929 --> 00:03:52.865
<i> I actually couldn't
 go anywhere. It was like
 holding--</i>

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.200 align:start size:66% position:34%
Oh, that makes sense,
you had a parachute
behind you...

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.768 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Yeah.
- ...at that point.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.103
Lisa:<i> So this is a great
 example of the four forces</i>

00:03:58.103 --> 00:03:59.605
<i> acting on you all at once.</i>

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:01.306
<i> You are trying to
 exert thrust on yourself</i>

00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:02.708
<i> by moving yourself forward.</i>

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:04.276
<i> You've got the drag
 of the wind</i>

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:05.711
<i> pushing on you
 trying to keep you back.</i>

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:06.946 line:0%
<i> You've got the weight
 of your body</i>

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.781 line:0%
<i> keeping you on the floor,</i>

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.783 line:0%
<i> and then the lift,
 you can actually see
 a little bit</i>

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:13.518
<i> in the parachute
 from your lab coat</i>

00:04:13.518 --> 00:04:17.457
and just that kind of lift 
and pushing up on your chest
as you lean forward, too.

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.658
So all of those forces
are acting on you at once

00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:21.126
even as the wind is blowing
in one direction.

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:22.662 align:start position:0%
I look like I'm totally
chilling there.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.464
Gav:<i> You're having the time
 of your life.</i>

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.865
Dan:<i> Usually, it's so much
 effort to do that,</i>

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.733
<i> but it was so easy
 because the wind.</i>

00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:29.702
<i> But now that it takes 80 miles
 an hour to do that for me.</i>

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.504 align:end position:100%
And now I've gone
for a jump here.
By me jumping forwards,

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.006 align:start size:91% position:9%
I went almost straight up
and came back down like this.

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:35.774 align:start position:0%
Wow, you'd be so late
for school.

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:36.675
( laughter )

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:38.277
Gav:
<i> If I had a lab coat on</i>

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:39.579
<i> and I walking through that
 to school,</i>

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:41.113 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I wouldn't get there.
- Yeah. ( laughs )

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:42.815
Lisa:<i> Couldn't make it.</i>

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:48.020
Gav:<i> Uh, this was actually
 the scariest thing that I did.</i>

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.088
<i> I was wondering
 what would happen
 if I went on the floor.</i>

00:04:50.088 --> 00:04:51.924
<i> But as soon as I held up
 my lab coat like a parachute.</i>

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.259
Lisa:<i> Yup.</i>

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.593 align:start position:0%
It just started sucking me
along the floor.

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:57.563 align:start position:0%
And I got some significant
distance here.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.565
<i> See, here's me, I've got--
 I'm going too fast.</i>

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.567 align:start position:0%
So I've put it down
and I'm still,

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:06.472 align:start size:91% position:9%
- the momentum is still--
  um, is still--
- ( laughter )

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:09.842
Apologies for that.
No one wants to see that.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.978 align:start size:72% position:28%
So why don't we move on
to a little table top
experiment?

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:17.283 align:start position:0%
So we've been to
a multi-million pound
wind tunnel in England

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:19.284 align:start position:0%
and now for our table top
experiment,

00:05:19.284 --> 00:05:20.586 align:start position:0%
we've got a little
wind tunnel

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:23.188 align:start position:0%
that didn't cost
millions of pounds.

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:25.391 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Multi-pounds?
- Multi-pounds, though.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.725 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Yeah.
- Can't get it for a quid.

00:05:26.725 --> 00:05:28.761 align:start position:0%
It's just a normal fan
with a tube,

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:32.064 align:start position:0%
a bunch of tape,
and a lovely clear
wind tunnel area.

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:33.499 align:start position:0%
So we can test out
these two cars.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.402 align:start position:0%
We got an old boxy one,
and a lovely streamlined one.

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:39.805 align:start size:78% position:22%
Because we can't see air,
so we want to know
what's gonna happen,

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:41.440 align:start size:47% position:53%
we've got this
vaporizer here,

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.575 align:start size:69% position:31%
which is gonna create
a bit of smoke for us.

00:05:43.575 --> 00:05:45.277 align:start size:72% position:28%
I'm gonna shove it in
and hopefully we'll see

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:47.479 align:start size:69% position:31%
the smoke going around
the cars in different
patterns.

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:49.315
Gav: Why don't we start
with the boxy one.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:51.150 align:start size:72% position:28%
What is your prediction
for this then?

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.918
I'm not thinking
it's very aerodynamic.

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:54.119 align:start size:84% position:16%
- ( laughter )
- You're probably just
  gonna see

00:05:54.119 --> 00:05:55.922
smoke going everywhere.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:58.290
( machine buzzing )

00:05:58.290 --> 00:05:59.959 align:start position:0%
Yeah, you can see it
just bashing against

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:01.627
the wind-screen there.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:04.764
Lisa: Yeah, that blunt front
is not doing it any favors.

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:06.231
Gav:
Shall we try the second one?

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:08.501 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah.
- A little bit bigger.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.169 align:start position:0%
But we'll pretend that
it's the exact same size.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.570 align:start size:31% position:69%
( scoffs )

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.572
Gav: All right, I'll give it
some action.

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:14.240
( machine buzzing )

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.142
Lisa: So for this one
you can actually see
the smoke

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.376 align:start size:84% position:16%
- rising over the top.
- Gav: Yeah.

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:18.744
It's coming all the way
back here,

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:20.346
and then it's coming down
at the end.

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:23.116
Exactly. This car is much
better designed

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:24.817
for fuel economy
than the old car.

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:28.187
And this way you save drag,
and when you save drag,

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:30.522
you save gas,
and when you save gas,
you save money.

00:06:30.522 --> 00:06:32.191 align:start position:0%
What's the weirdest stuff
you've put into a wind tunnel?

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.658
Some of the oddest things
I've seen

00:06:33.658 --> 00:06:35.328
would have to be
a trash can.

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:36.862 align:start size:59% position:41%
Why would you need
a trash can to be--

00:06:36.862 --> 00:06:38.464 align:start position:0%
Is it to stop
from blowing away
in the wind?

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:39.665
Exactly, you don't want it
rolling down...

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.200
Gav: Actually makes
total sense.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.634
...once you've put it
on the street.

00:06:42.634 --> 00:06:44.236 align:start size:88% position:13%
Actually, I've got something
I want to put in here.

00:06:44.236 --> 00:06:47.907 align:start size:56% position:44%
Thinking about it,
hang on.

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.908 align:start size:91% position:9%
- Us.
- Oh, us from episode one.

00:06:49.908 --> 00:06:51.444 align:start size:16% position:84%
Yeah.

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:54.380 align:start size:63% position:38%
Obviously, I assume
I'm going to be less
aerodynamic.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.715 align:start size:97% position:3%
- ( chuckles )
- Let's put me slightly there

00:06:56.715 --> 00:06:57.917 align:start size:88% position:13%
- and you slightly off.
- Okay.

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.352
( machine buzzing )

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:00.620
Gav: Oh, yeah, it's coming
around you,

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.088
It's going through
your arm holes.

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:04.023
Dan: It just goes
like nothing through you.

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:06.091 align:start size:91% position:9%
- ( Gav laughs )
- Dan: It just completely
  avoids you.

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:09.128
Gav: Do you learn the same
information from doing it
